## 2. Qualys VMDR (Vulnerability Management, Detection & Response)

**Type:** Commercial, cloud-based, agent + agentless platform.

**What it does:** Continuous asset discovery, vulnerability detection, prioritization (using a "Qualys Detection Score"/real-time threat intelligence), and patch orchestration â€” all from a centralized cloud dashboard, ideal for large distributed enterprises and hybrid cloud.

**Strengths:**
- Continuous (not just point-in-time) scanning via lightweight cloud agents installed on assets
- Built-in compliance and asset-inventory modules
- Prioritizes vulnerabilities using real-world exploit-likelihood data, not just CVSS score

**Example use case:**
- An enterprise deploys the **Qualys Cloud Agent** on 5,000 endpoints (laptops, cloud VMs). Instead of scheduling scans, the agent continuously reports posture back to the Qualys cloud platform.
- When a new critical CVE is disclosed (e.g., a widely-exploited Apache Log4j-style vulnerability), VMDR automatically flags every affected asset across the entire fleet within minutes and generates a prioritized remediation ticket list, ranked by "real-time threat" indicators (active exploitation in the wild) rather than raw severity alone.

