## 5. Acunetix

**Type:** Commercial, automated **DAST** (Dynamic Application Security Testing) â€” specifically web-application focused.

**What it does:** Crawls and actively tests web applications and APIs for vulnerabilities, with strong out-of-the-box detection specifically tuned to the OWASP Top 10 (SQLi, XSS, misconfig, outdated components, etc.).

**Strengths:**
- Very low false-positive rate for high-risk web vulns thanks to "proof-based" scanning (it attempts to safely prove exploitability rather than just flag patterns)
- Good coverage of modern JavaScript-heavy single-page applications (SPAs)
- Built-in compliance reporting (PCI-DSS mapping)

**Example use case:**
- A dev team points Acunetix at their staging e-commerce site (`https://staging.shop.example.com`). It crawls every page/form, then tests the checkout form's "promo code" field, and reports a confirmed SQL injection vulnerability (A03) with the exact payload used and a proof-of-concept showing extracted database version info â€” letting the team fix it before the site goes to production.

