## 7. OWASP ZAP (Zed Attack Proxy)

**Type:** Free, open-source â€” maintained under the OWASP umbrella, positioned as the free alternative/entry point to Burp Suite.

**What it does:** Intercepting proxy + automated active/passive scanner, designed to be integrated into the SDLC (developers running it themselves, not just security teams) and into CI/CD pipelines.

**Strengths:**
- Completely free and scriptable â€” great for developers and small teams without a Burp Pro license
- Has both a GUI (Desktop) and a **headless/CLI mode** perfect for automation
- Passive scanning happens automatically as you browse the app (no active attack needed) â€” good early warning with zero risk

**Example use case:**
```bash
# Running a ZAP baseline scan in a CI pipeline (headless, Docker)
docker run -t owasp/zap2docker-stable zap-baseline.py \
  -t https://staging.example.com \
  -r zap_report.html
```
- A dev team adds this ZAP baseline scan as a step in their GitHub Actions pipeline. On every pull request to staging, ZAP passively crawls the app and fails the build if it detects missing security headers or newly introduced reflected XSS â€” catching issues before they reach production.

